<section id="income-level-segmentation">
<h2>6. Fuel Affordability by Income Level</h2>
<p>Countries are classified into three GNI-per-capita tiers: <b>High</b> (32 countries), <b>Middle</b> (29), and <b>Low</b> (23). Paradoxically, High-income countries pay the most for fuel in absolute terms — because they also levy the highest taxes and are concentrated in the Low-subsidy tier.</p>

<div class="card">
  <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="incomeChart"></canvas></div>
</div>

<table>
